  <reporting-org ref="XM-DAC-41302" type="40">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">International Labour Organization (ILO)</narrative>
  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">increased capacities of constituents to implement productive employment and decent work policies and programmes</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Namibia continues to face structurally high levels of unemployment, with disproportionately higher rates among young women and men. These challenges are compounded by persistent labour market inequalities, skills mismatches and limited access to decent and productive employment opportunities. Addressing unemployment and promoting inclusive growth is therefore central to Namibia&#x2019;s Sixth National Development Plan (NDP6), which prioritizes economic diversification, job creation, human capital development and strengthened social protection systems. In this context, Namibia&#x2019;s participation in the UN Global Accelerator on Jobs and Social Protection for Just Transitions further reinforces national efforts by aligning employment creation with expanded social protection coverage to support a more inclusive and resilient labour market.
The ILO supports the Government of Namibia and its social partners in advancing employment-centered economic and investment policies that foster full, productive and decent employment. This includes the formulation of a comprehensive employment policy frameworks, mainstreaming employment objectives into national development planning processes, and promoting coherence across macroeconomic (fiscal and monetary policies), sectoral, labour market and investment policies.
The strategy combines technical assistance for employment diagnostics and employment impact assessments with support for improved labour market governance, skills development systems and targeted informal economy (facilitating the transition to formality) and youth employment interventions. In addition, the ILO support seeks to enhance inter-ministerial coordination and strengthen social dialogue mechanisms. Emphasis is placed on the design and implementation of youth employment strategies, programmes and action plans in collaboration with tripartite constituents and development partners, ensuring alignment with both NDP6 priorities and the objectives of the Global Accelerator.</narrative>
  </description>
